{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121512","id":4079071748,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7zIbIE","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121512","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121512.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121512.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121512","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121512/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121512/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121512/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/712265242c85038791390b446f7346ba7757526b","number":121512,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Some fixes for boolean conversion in shaders","user":{"login":"Chaosus","id":3036176,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzYxNzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3036176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus","html_url":"https://github.com/Chaosus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chaosus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is a continuation of a recent [PR](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120715) which enables to transform booleans to scalar in a shader language. \r\nFirst, I've makes the operators been treated like a constant statement, so this code will compile correctly now:\r\n\r\n```gdshader\r\nvoid fragment() {\r\n\tvec3 v = vec3(1 == 1);\r\n\r\n\t// or\r\n\r\n\tvec3 v2 = vec3(true ? 1 : 0);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI've also found that a conversion between boolean scalar is allowed only in built-in type constructors (in GLSL). \r\nRead also: https://github.khronos.org/Vulkan-Site/glsl/latest/chapters/operators.html#constructors\r\nSo after this PR got merged user allowed to use boolean conversion only in cases like that:\r\n\r\n```gdshader\r\nvoid fragment()\r\n{\r\n\tvec3 v = vec3(1 == 1, true, 0);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd these cases will be forbidden:\r\n\r\n```gdshader\r\nvoid foo(float a) {\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid fragment() {\r\n    foo(true);\r\n\tabs(true);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1609442062,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjA5NDQyMDYy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:shaders","name":"topic:shaders","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","number":25,"state":"open","title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/fol